%YAML 1.2
# Example .pages for mkdocs-awesome-pages-plugin
# Rename this file to `.pages` in `chapters/` to enable manual control
# of the navigation. This is optional — the repository includes an automatic
# `scripts/generate_mkdocs_nav.py` that builds `mkdocs.yml` from filenames
# and titles. Use `.pages` only if you want explicit, hand-maintained order.

title: "Manual de Opciones Financieras"
pages:
  - "Introducción & Fundamentos":
    - 00-introduccion.md
    - 01-como-piensan-los-gestores.md
    - 02-fundamentos.md

  - "Estrategias y conceptos prácticos":
    - 10-leaps.md
    - 11-bull-put-spread.md
    - 12-bull-call-spread.md
    # ... añade las páginas en el orden exacto que quieras mostrar

  - "Nivel profesional, modelos y frameworks (100–199)":
    - 100-diagonal-spread.md
    - 101-iron-condor-profesional.md

  - "Checklists, glosario y anexos (200+)":
    - 200-checklist-profesional-previo-a-cada-operacion.md
    - 211-glosario-profesional.md

# Notes:
# - The YAML above is just an example. If you rename to `.pages`, awesome-pages
#   will use this to construct the sidebar. Keep the filenames relative to this
#   directory.
# - Use `.pages` when you need fine-grained control. Otherwise rely on the
#   autogenerated `mkdocs.yml` (via scripts/generate_mkdocs_nav.py).

